===Noun===
{{wikipedia}}
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|computing}} A [[desktop]] [[computer]], normally more [[powerful]] than a normal [[PC]] and often [[dedicated]] to a specific [[task]], such as [[graphics]].
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2021 October 20|author=Paul Stephen|title=Leisure and pleasure on the Far North Line: Radio Electronic Token Block|journal=RAIL|issue=942|page=48|text=All train movements on the Far North Line have been controlled by a Radio Electronic Token Block '''workstation''' at Inverness since 1995, having already been introduced on the Kyle Line some 11 years earlier.}}
# An [[area]], at a [[workplace]], for a single [[worker]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2010| title=Slow Horses|author=Mick Herron| page=299| passage=Lamb ignored her, surveying her team instead, who were at their own or each other's '''workstations''', and engrossed in their current tasks, and studying every move he made.}}

